\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-9|\\begin{aligned}0 & -8 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8)-9(-16) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda -72)+144 & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda +72 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37396/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37396"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86758/selection/7cd7342fadab9762c78ceb65401c5215cd33bc98ace3c8b1e7ca74eec127fc17" :answer/id #uuid "c0046a85-aaf9-5ddc-86d6-624075345a6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86758/selection/20a268c9942e21aacb8003c11d5ee6d30dad32be0169dc08f076672a76b73099" :answer/id #uuid "8ea45ba8-3eac-5207-8bc7-2d0e02c70b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86758/selection/dd511d60a1794f439093b319940d583ea17853341fe183a2c73996f492d81bd5" :answer/id #uuid "a6e22436-50f0-5d3c-8827-b21fe19d0a39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {2,-1,1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86758/selection/ad0f7e9dd132b0909d380e24ebe462830d1ef6f065aad165b5e46858ca3d63ad" :answer/id #uuid "d38ebc87-e8af-57d0-a9aa-f88cd14aaffb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-1,1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86758/selection/b28e83a2d10d87b1a4923f4b0aea4212c68fbdc675b657a683a16e4dfae85af2" :answer/id #uuid "f687f430-e93a-572e-ae24-706a454b6eb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1,1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86758/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4e47216-2ae5-5fec-ba60-2fa2e1a1d6fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86758/selection/b28e83a2d10d87b1a4923f4b0aea4212c68fbdc675b657a683a16e4dfae85af2" :answer-field/choices ["q-86758/selection/7cd7342fadab9762c78ceb65401c5215cd33bc98ace3c8b1e7ca74eec127fc17" "q-86758/selection/20a268c9942e21aacb8003c11d5ee6d30dad32be0169dc08f076672a76b73099" "q-86758/selection/dd511d60a1794f439093b319940d583ea17853341fe183a2c73996f492d81bd5" "q-86758/selection/ad0f7e9dd132b0909d380e24ebe462830d1ef6f065aad165b5e46858ca3d63ad" "q-86758/selection/b28e83a2d10d87b1a4923f4b0aea4212c68fbdc675b657a683a16e4dfae85af2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86758" :question/id #uuid "8b75d1ac-303a-511c-86a2-e86c1eaa7201" :question/math-academy-id "q-86758" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$O=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,O-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nO-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(O-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(O-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+1)+(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $2:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2\n$$\n\nLet's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}+2(1)^{2}-(1)-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is a root of the equation. So, we can factor $(\\lambda -1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86758/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86758"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37394/selection/55473ff20cd7e86d05a13757a5ee3ff98c19b83c0ac62da1429e6bcffd076af4" :answer/id #uuid "21780e5a-aa2d-5246-b77f-6480f36fd2b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-10{\\lambda }^{2}+43\\lambda -90=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37394/selection/c00bf6fc6a5acf172555de6075a179b4b207b4f2794988bb63f004bf6551adb9" :answer/id #uuid "796330cc-25f4-53aa-a572-e18b94cc160c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37394/selection/bceba0e6fc3f8048f2d6549c13a09cc54f4137993708773685eca1a7a17591fe" :answer/id #uuid "d49cabe9-38d2-5f98-a0d0-dbc3e9cfff65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+7{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -48=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37394/selection/c8b827a94704cd9bbd70d19385d055c573a276e686979dfa8c89e53c6e27bb7c" :answer/id #uuid "b19fdf67-ffd1-5ab2-a8fd-4bbec19a170f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -52=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37394/selection/397f6c488a303e059d964607223bc454236fbd19bb835eea2861fe360328048f" :answer/id #uuid "614d0399-6f7f-5355-a891-c40b97a89907" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+49\\lambda -138=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37394/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3523d308-a1c8-5c3e-a37f-455f1d5717a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37394/selection/c00bf6fc6a5acf172555de6075a179b4b207b4f2794988bb63f004bf6551adb9" :answer-field/choices ["q-37394/selection/55473ff20cd7e86d05a13757a5ee3ff98c19b83c0ac62da1429e6bcffd076af4" "q-37394/selection/c00bf6fc6a5acf172555de6075a179b4b207b4f2794988bb63f004bf6551adb9" "q-37394/selection/bceba0e6fc3f8048f2d6549c13a09cc54f4137993708773685eca1a7a17591fe" "q-37394/selection/c8b827a94704cd9bbd70d19385d055c573a276e686979dfa8c89e53c6e27bb7c" "q-37394/selection/397f6c488a303e059d964607223bc454236fbd19bb835eea2861fe360328048f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37394" :question/id #uuid "f99fb1fc-bc54-57d8-9eee-0c97852ae922" :question/math-academy-id "q-37394" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-8)|\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-4)|\\begin{aligned}3 & 8-\\lambda  \\\\ -6 & -10\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +6)+8(-3\\lambda +9)-4(-6\\lambda +18) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6)+(-24\\lambda +72)-(-24\\lambda +72) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37394/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37394"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5486"] :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda$ of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/9c2a25dabbe750ebb52b4de6dbee954df55c09a8ceaf0b82eef346b5a337c544.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/947389b453c22e1b56704ec6a1cdf8e7e529ea9a944c57d3e55a471ab3539569.png)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 9-\\lambda  & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )(9-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)(\\lambda -9)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda_1=-9,$ $\\lambda_2=9,$ and $\\lambda_3=6.$ \n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7047"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/2379f9f0cec3f257da5a4c0695f114d0bc7f3b4c914edabfd690ff94705faceb.png)\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\lambda=4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- $\\lambda=-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- The eigenvalue $\\lambda=6$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, P-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/8ee9ef991440e5641d6a458c0384382b54eb3d8504856b942fc33cf24b0b85e9.png)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(P-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4 \\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3 \\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-\\lambda )\\cdot (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 7 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )((-1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-35) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda=3,$ $\\lambda=4,$ $\\lambda=6,$ and $\\lambda=-6$ (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5487"] :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/dc652e29fc17e565962d96a947980358f776d5e37816269dbe9139328889fc3f.png) of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/a93a99c9a1491b842d5b8d30c90f37b06528d0bd1b82bb5257d84ecb43a2b288.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/0d5fcfb7528ad4e3fcf0e7f173d9bd0be80d5148b6c1bda8a9bb765dc772d1e2.png)\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/619fe52f77e282e97915de285e8384d784dc6352eb06295e6991a1bdb2bae1c3.png)\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/02f21e39c78b5ad8b88c5040d074fe78a5e6950760f2653b724c4e27627752ba.png) \n\nExpanding the determinant across the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/ac192f9c9318b0668e9dee7e695d4dd383f2d74df0298ef6dd4861d421e97afb.png)st row, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/7062cb3cf1cf9e2dc2cac6c69537dd6c20c5b211f641a511092d7fbf8457d9de.png)\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/97622f2aa4af27b2ce48c21c48e49129b58197dd2d02a3dddb5ff3685ba8197e.png) \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/a40f8317b6de6727323c39a9e8105822544f88727eb855ce5e89c71cc185c485.png)\n\nLet's pick ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/4b7d6cca59677b4ec63fc9997d5d32c4d2e67f87d45b89540e42293f4ed1ba73.png) Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/146529d47426ad676072aeba20837a6da7ea5dc400a17f37dd3cb4d0a5c7f107.png)\nSo, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/f161fa211fd6dda217ad08855ed96703b8f620aeb1485d67562f3bf1666928d7.png) is a root of the equation. This means we can factor ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/210f39779d00613e2fcc094145f31e789ae93a0361618ae6b4623c107272799f.png) out of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/b8b832cc07ffad66665f2b961a9d78d97a0a89caac7ffc765e065a6d0946d0f6.png) using synthetic division:\n\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/124a84b4788cb014c01f416a1e0433eb7991fd3c4c792400892377f4f3407221.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069304/assets/e12ac0c95825bef841bc95fa94b20bf787e03ec405c223a26fab4a73c61efa10.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/line